│ of those side effects. There were 50 patients in the informed (study) group and 48 patients in the uninformed        │
│ (control) group. The informed group received counselling about particular side effects, while the uninformed group   │
│ received no information about particular side effects of the same drug. All patients received the identical form and │
│ dose of erythromycin dispensed by the physician, avoiding possible consultation with a pharmacist. Informed patients │
│ were told that the medication was safe but that abdominal cramps and discomfort were frequent side effects, while    │
│ nausea, vomiting, loss of appetite, and diarrhea were less frequent. The uninformed group was given no information   │
